% General overview on hiearchical clustering and some related algorithms which
% seek to partitions a given data into hiearchical subsets either from totally
% partitioned sets of elements up until the elements as a single set, or vice
% versa. Agglomerated hierarchical cluster is a set partition where partition
% boundaries (elements on a line), or equivalently non-terminating roots of a
% tree-like hierarchy (bifurcation points in a dendrogram) represent a decision
% treshold that guides where set extraneous objects are to categorized into.
%
% tags: agglomerative hierarchical clustering algorithm
%
